course: dictionary
lesson: 9691
title: The right to vote
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Suffrage means the right to vote in elections. «Suffrage means the right to vote» tells you the meaning straight away, so you can use it when you meet the word in a text.
explain: Other words near suffrage show who gets the right. Women's suffrage means women's right to vote. Universal suffrage means all adult citizens can vote. Ask yourself: who is being given the vote?
explain: People who campaigned for votes were called suffragists and suffragettes. Their work for women's votes is known as the suffrage movement, and it often took many years.
fact: Suffrage means the right to vote in elections.
fact: «New Zealand gave women the vote in 1893, the USA in 1920.»
fact: In the UK, some women got the vote in 1918, and women gained equal suffrage with men in 1928.
fact: Black Americans and many others also fought for a long time for equal suffrage.
fact: "Women's suffrage" and "universal suffrage" are common phrases, and suffrage is usually used without "a" or "the" when you mean the idea of voting.
exercise: «Suffrage means the right to vote; New Zealand gave women the vote in 1893.» What does suffrage mean? | *The right to vote | The right to rule the country | A school for children | A kind of ship
exercise: What does "women's suffrage" mean? | Women's right to a holiday | Women's right to lead the army | Women's right to be a judge | *Women's right to vote
exercise: What does "universal suffrage" mean? | Nobody is allowed to vote | Children can vote | *All adult citizens can vote | Only the richest people can vote
test: Which phrase means all adult citizens can vote? | Suffrage movement | *Universal suffrage | Women's suffrage
test: In which year did New Zealand give women the vote? | 1918 | 1920 | *1893 | 1928
exam: In the UK, women gained equal suffrage with men in which year? | *1928 | 1918 | 1893 | 1920
